// Formative practice quiz for sharing-state-with-context. Low-stakes; answers are visible by design. First draft, not yet reviewed.
$CATEGORY: react/forms-context-and-crud/sharing-state-with-context

::sharing-state-with-context o1 - nearest provider::Two providers of the same context are nested, and a component below both calls useContext. Which value does it get?{
=The value from the nearest provider above it#Correct. The closest one wins.
~The value from the top provider#Not quite. The inner one overrides it for its subtree.
~The default value#Not quite. The default is used only when no provider is above.
~An array of both#Not quite. useContext returns one value.
}

::sharing-state-with-context o1 - create location::Where is createContext normally called?{
=Outside any component, often in its own module#Correct. A context is a single shared object, so it should not be recreated by renders.
~Inside each component that reads it#Not quite. That would make a new context each time, so nothing would connect.
~Inside useEffect#Not quite. Nothing about it needs an Effect.
~In index.html#Not quite. That file holds no React code.
}

::sharing-state-with-context o2 - context re-render::A provider value changes because App state changed. What happens to a deep component that calls useContext for it?{
=It re-renders with the new value#Correct. A changed context value is a re-render trigger.
~It keeps the old value until the page reloads#Not quite. Readers update as soon as the value changes.
~It only updates if it receives a prop too#Not quite. No prop is needed.
~It unmounts#Not quite. It stays mounted and re-renders.
}

::sharing-state-with-context o3 - good fit::Which data is the best fit for context?{
=The signed-in user, needed by many components at different depths#Correct. Widely needed data is what context is for.
~A label passed from a parent to its child#Not quite. A prop is simpler and clearer for that.
~The text in one input#Not quite. Local state is enough.
~A value computed inside one component#Not quite. Compute it locally. Nothing else needs it.
}
